= The Picasso File and the Responsability Comission

The Parliamentary Comission of Responsability has been created to continue with the General Picasso's exhaustive report. This investigation could expose corruption inside the high ranks of the army. We could limit ourself to honor the memory of our fallen soldiers, demand justice for them or extend the inquiry to the crimes commited during Primo de Rivera's Dictatorship.

- @restart: Restart the inquiry.
- @root: Do nothing.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@restart
on-arrival: war_guilt += 1

What is the goal of this tribunal?

- @pure_history: To provide a historical record of the events of the war and honor our fallen soldiers.
- @limit: To demand justice and responsabilities for the Disaster of Annual and the whole Rif war.
- @rewrite: To demand justice and responsabilties for the Rif war and the Dictatorship. We are going against the old guard both in the army and in the state.

@pure_history
on-arrival: polarization -= 5; coup_progress -= 1; caballeristas_dissent += 10; prietistas_dissent += 10; besteiristas_dissent += 10; pro_republic -= 5; ar_relation -= 10; prr_relation -= 10; prrs_relation -= 10

We avoid diggnig up past military failures and convert the comission into a solemn state tribute to the soldiers killed in Africa with symbolic trials. While this appeases the conservatives and the military, our republican allies view it as a cowardly movement. The discontent grows inside our ranks aswell.  

@limit
on-arrival: polarization += 3; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.1; pro_republic += 3

We restrict the comission to investigate negligence and corruption during the Rif War. King Alfonso XIII is condemned for high treason and Dámaso Berenguer is also found guilty. The results are mostly the same as general Picasso's, satisfaying moderate republicans and avoiding excesive public backslash. However, army officers feel targeted, lowering their approval of the new regime.


@rewrite
on-arrival: polarization += 7; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.2; pro_republic += 7; coup_progress += 1; workers_psoe += 2; rural_psoe += 3;

We need to continue Picasso's File and extend it to the corruption and crimes of the dictatorship. By doing this we've targeted both the Africanist and Peninsular military leadership. King Alfonso XIII is condemned for high treason and Dámaso Berenguer is also found guilty. This way we've solodified the republican legitimacy at the cost of alienating the army leadership completely.
